[
  {
    "text": "High-NA EUV systems have a half-field size of 26 mm x 16.5 mm, which is insufficient for full-chip logic and DRAM die sizes without stitching, regardless of design strategies.",
    "topic": "field-size limitation"
  },
  {
    "text": "Innovative design strategies such as 3D stacking or chiplet partitioning can circumvent the field-size limitation, but these are not a direct replacement for monolithic stitching-free exposure.",
    "topic": "design strategy scope"
  },
  {
    "text": "Edge placement error of <1 nm for stitching-free high-NA EUV has only been demonstrated on test structures with relaxed design rules, not on production logic or DRAM patterns.",
    "topic": "EPE demonstration scope"
  },
  {
    "text": "DRAM cell arrays have regular pitches that may be aligned to avoid stitching boundaries through sub-array partitioning, but logic standard cells with random placement cannot avoid stitching without severe area penalty.",
    "topic": "logic vs. DRAM layout regularity"
  }
]
